WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:15.628
When Mead finally arrived from New York, Dr.

2
00:00:15.668 --> 00:00:17.449
Warren drove him to the Harrington house.

3
00:00:19.571 --> 00:00:23.213
Aunt Polly introduced the specialist to Pollyanna and Miss Hunt, the nurse.

4
00:00:23.233 --> 00:00:25.574
"I like you, Dr.

5
00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:28.256
Mead!" Pollyanna said after he examined her.

6
00:00:30.004 --> 00:00:32.425
"Maybe it's because you look a lot like my doctor."

7
00:00:32.445 --> 00:00:35.307
"Your doctor?"

8
00:00:36.668 --> 00:00:37.989
Dr. Mead looked at Dr.

9
00:00:38.029 --> 00:00:39.890
Warren, who was talking to the nurse.

10
00:00:41.831 --> 00:00:44.532
Dr. Warren was a small man with a brown beard.

11
00:00:46.173 --> 00:00:48.814
Dr. Mead was a tall man with a cheerful smile.

12
00:00:48.834 --> 00:00:51.316
"But we don't look anything alike!"

13
00:00:53.417 --> 00:00:54.778
Pollyanna glanced at Dr.

14
00:00:54.798 --> 00:00:58.480
Warren. "Oh, he isn't my doctor.

15
00:00:59.628 --> 00:01:01.769
Dr. Warren is Aunt Polly's doctor.

16
00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:04.451
My doctor is Dr.

17
00:01:04.511 --> 00:01:07.052
Chilton." At the mention of Dr.

18
00:01:07.092 --> 00:01:08.933
Chilton, Aunt Polly turned red.

19
00:01:08.953 --> 00:01:12.075
"You see, I wanted Dr.

20
00:01:12.115 --> 00:01:15.137
Chilton right from the beginning," Pollyanna went on.

21
00:01:15.157 --> 00:01:17.818
"But Aunt Polly wanted you.

22
00:01:18.759 --> 00:01:20.079
She said you knew more than Dr.

23
00:01:20.139 --> 00:01:22.221
Chilton did about broken legs like mine.

24
00:01:23.581 --> 00:01:26.203
Of course, if you do, then I'll be glad about that.

25
00:01:26.823 --> 00:01:27.824
So, do you?"

26
00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:31.661
"Only time will tell, young lady," Dr.

27
00:01:31.721 --> 00:01:32.742
Mead said gently.

28
00:01:33.923 --> 00:01:36.964
His smile had disappeared, and he looked quite serious.

29
00:01:36.984 --> 00:01:41.827
"Now, if everyone else could join me in the hall, I'd like to speak to you."

30
00:01:45.589 --> 00:01:47.931
What happened next upset everyone in the house.

31
00:01:49.792 --> 00:01:53.774
As the adults talked in the hall, Fluffy, the cat, poked at Pollyanna's door.

32
00:01:54.794 --> 00:01:57.276
If the door had been closed, she would not have succeeded.

33
00:01:58.392 --> 00:02:02.695
But Fluffy managed to use her nose and paw to push the door until it stood ajar.

34
00:02:04.256 --> 00:02:07.858
The cat jumped onto the bed, just as Aunt Polly gave an anguished cry.

35
00:02:07.878 --> 00:02:11.401
"Not that!

36
00:02:12.201 --> 00:02:12.902
Oh, Dr.

37
00:02:12.962 --> 00:02:14.383
Mead, anything but that.

38
00:02:14.963 --> 00:02:19.506
You don't mean Aunt Polly had to force herself to say the awful words.

39
00:02:19.526 --> 00:02:23.629
"You don't mean she'll never walk again!"

40
00:02:27.211 --> 00:02:30.017
From the bedroom Pollyanna cried out in terror.

41
00:02:30.037 --> 00:02:31.458
"Aunt Polly!

42
00:02:31.478 --> 00:02:32.319
Aunt Polly!"

43
00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:39.483
Seeing the open door and realizing Pollyanna had overheard, Aunt Polly gave a low moan.

44
00:02:42.345 --> 00:02:45.027
Then, for the first time in her life, she fainted.

45
00:02:46.328 --> 00:02:47.389
Fortunately, Dr.

46
00:02:47.449 --> 00:02:49.190
Mead caught her before she hit the floor.

47
00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:52.172
"I'm coming, Pollyanna!"

48
00:02:53.992 --> 00:02:58.316
Miss Hunt stumbled toward the open door while the two doctors tended to Aunt Polly.

49
00:02:59.817 --> 00:03:04.521
In Pollyanna's room Fluffy was vainly trying to attract the panicked child's attention.

50
00:03:04.541 --> 00:03:08.704
"Miss Hunt, please, I want Aunt Polly."

51
00:03:09.765 --> 00:03:11.687
Pollyanna's eyes were wide with fear.

52
00:03:11.707 --> 00:03:14.009
"I want her right now.

53
00:03:14.409 --> 00:03:16.270
Quick, please get her for me!"

54
00:03:17.832 --> 00:03:19.873
The nurse closed the door and hurried over to the bed.

55
00:03:19.893 --> 00:03:22.676
"She can't come just this minute, dear.

56
00:03:23.124 --> 00:03:24.204
She will come a little later.

57
00:03:25.105 --> 00:03:25.725
What do you want?

58
00:03:26.165 --> 00:03:27.665
Is there something I can get for you?"

59
00:03:28.906 --> 00:03:29.986
Pollyanna shook her head.

60
00:03:30.006 --> 00:03:33.307
"I want to know more about what she just said.

61
00:03:33.327 --> 00:03:34.967
Did you hear her?

62
00:03:35.808 --> 00:03:36.768
I want Aunt Polly.

63
00:03:37.088 --> 00:03:40.129
She said something, and I need her to tell me it isn't true."

64
00:03:41.469 --> 00:03:44.130
Miss Hunt tried to speak but couldn't find the right words.

65
00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:48.311
Something in the nurse's face added to Pollyanna's terror.

66
00:03:48.331 --> 00:03:51.232
"Miss Hunt, you did hear her!

67
00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:53.181
It is true!

68
00:03:53.701 --> 00:03:56.183
You mean, I'll never walk again?"

69
00:03:56.203 --> 00:04:01.888
"There, there, dear, don't—" The nurse choked back her own tears.

70
00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:04.090
"Maybe Dr.

71
00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.671
Mead didn't know what he was saying.

72
00:04:06.311 --> 00:04:07.713
Perhaps he was mistaken.

73
00:04:08.753 --> 00:04:10.074
Lots of things could happen."

74
00:04:10.094 --> 00:04:16.399
"But Aunt Polly said he knew more than anybody else about broken legs like mine!"

75
00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:21.664
"Yes, I know, but all doctors make mistakes sometimes.

76
00:04:22.784 --> 00:04:24.786
Don't think anything more about it right now."

77
00:04:27.307 --> 00:04:29.029
Pollyanna flung out her arms.

78
00:04:29.049 --> 00:04:34.173
"But I can't help thinking about it," she sobbed.

79
00:04:34.193 --> 00:04:37.475
"It's all I can think about.

80
00:04:38.596 --> 00:04:41.678
How will I go to school or visit my friends?

81
00:04:42.719 --> 00:04:47.526
If I can't walk, how will I ever be glad about anything?"

82
00:04:49.167 --> 00:04:52.650
While Pollyanna sobbed, Miss Hunt had been preparing some medicine.

83
00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:56.432
"Just take this, dear," she said.

84
00:04:56.452 --> 00:05:00.295
"Maybe after you rest, things will seem brighter."

85
00:05:03.257 --> 00:05:06.579
Pollyanna took the medicine and sipped the water offered by Miss Hunt.

86
00:05:06.599 --> 00:05:10.001
"That sounds like something Father used to say.

87
00:05:10.762 --> 00:05:13.904
But he'd never been told he wouldn't walk again.

88
00:05:15.368 --> 00:05:17.670
Nothing could be worse than that, could it?"

89
00:05:19.751 --> 00:05:22.233
Miss Hunt had no answer for Pollyanna's question.
